-- title:
--   Every two-torsion translate remains in the square fibre
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a finite abelian group, $N=|G|$, $H=G[2]=\{u:2u=0\}$, $h=|H|$, $t=|G[3]|$, and $D=|2G|$. Write $R_S(z)$ for the ordered pair-sum count of a finite support $S$, $F(S)=\{T:|T|=3,R_T=R_S\}$, $O(S)=\{S+u:u\in H\}$, and $F^*=\{S\in F:0\notin S\}$. Ordinary full fibres have size $h$, exceptional full fibres size $2h$. All displayed subtractions are natural subtraction, truncated at zero, and all quotients are integer division. For every support $S$ of size three,
--
--   $$O(S)\subseteq F(S).$$
--
--   Translations by elements killed by two preserve all ordered pair-sum counts.
-- source:
--   Alexandre Couret, Couret — Additive reconstruction: STROBO-4, singleton collisions and RECOH formal proof artifacts, https://zenodo.org/records/23980513; archive COURET_MATHEMATIQUES_20261105.zip, SHA-256 19a3b59aee930df74cab79c27b29e014843bd17179a26fef1261ed6b5a651ab7; file RECOH/lean/Strobo2TorsCardinality.lean, lines 202–209; source file SHA-256 43bb7bc977683362729a3aa2f7c214abefd9138f3283fb79ee93f0a1da784093; theorem Couret.STROBO2TORS.torsionOrbit_subset_fibre

